<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Velu Thampi Dalawa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1809">1809</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Velu Thampi Dalawa was the chief minister, or dalawa, of the kingdom of Travancore from 1802 to 1809. After reforming its administration and finances, he clashed with the British Resident over the subsidy demanded under the treaty of 1805, and in 1809 he led an armed revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, announced in his Kundara Proclamation. When it failed he killed himself to avoid capture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/velu-thampi-dalawa.jpg" alt="Velu Thampi Dalawa" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiran Gopi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Veluthampi.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
